  "title": "Overcoming ‘faster horses’ thinking in DTC AI audience targeting",
  "summary": "Whether or not Henry Ford actually said “If I’d asked people what they wanted, they would’ve said ‘faster horses’” is debatable. And yet I think about that quote often, because it captures something deeply human: the instinct to improve what we already know rather than question whether we’re solving the right problem. It’s classic “if it ain’t broke” thinking. And I see it everywhere in how our industry is approaching […]",
